  "combinedHtml": "<!-- block: About Automatic Patterning on this Machine | HTML 9332 -->\n<style>.circle{\r\nwidth:25px;\r\nheight:25px;\r\nborder-radius:50%;\r\nbox-sizing:border-box;\r\ntext-align:center;\r\ndisplay:inline-block;\r\nline-height:25px;\r\nbackground-color:#9F2065;\r\n}\r\n.circle a{\r\ntext-decoration:none;\r\ncolor:#fff;\r\nfont-size: 16px;\r\n}\r\n.container-border1 {\r\nborder: 2px solid #ccc;\r\nborder-radius: 15px 50px;\r\npadding-top: 20px;\r\npadding-right: 20px;\r\npadding-bottom: 20px;\r\npadding-left: 20px;\r\nbackground-color: white;\r\n}</style>\r\n<style> .container-border1 {\r\nborder: 2px solid #ccc;\r\nborder-radius: 15px 50px;\r\npadding-top: 20px;\r\npadding-right: 20px;\r\npadding-bottom: 20px;\r\npadding-left: 20px;\r\nbackground-color: white;\r\nmax-width: 500px;\r\nmargin: auto;\r\nbackground-color: #DCDCDC;\r\n}\r\n</style>\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-sm-7 col-xs-12\">\r\nAlmost magical, stitch patterning on this machine can happen in 2 ways:<br><br>\r\n\r\n\r\n<a href=\"#demo\" data-toggle=\"collapse\">\r\n<div class=\"circle\"><a href=\"#\">1</a></div> <span style=\"font-size:1.5em\"><a data-GlossaryId=\"730\" class=\"glossaryhelp\">EC1 / PE1 Pattern Controller </a><i class=\"fa fa-caret-down\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i></span> <br><br>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<em>This course does not include instruction on using the EC1 device</em><br><br>\r\n\r\n</a>\r\n<div id=\"demo\" class=\"collapse hidden-print\">\r\nLorem ipsum dolor text....\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"circle\"><a href=\"#\">2</a></div> <span style=\"font-size:1.5em\">DesignaKnit</span><br><br>\r\nCreate and Integrate stitch patterns in DesignaKnit. Using Interactive knitting, DAK sends your pattern information to a \"translator\" SilverLink Box, which in turn send zeros and ones to your carriage instructing it to select and de-select needles.<br>\r\n<br><br><h3><em>NOTE: The <a data-GlossaryId=\"728\" class=\"glossaryhelp\">N-1 Cams (Needle 1) <i class=\"fa fa-question-circle\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i></a> are NOT used with DesignaKnit</em></h3>\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"col-sm-5 col-xs-12\"><div class=\"container-border1\">Textured stitch patterns and multi-color patterns can all be quickly produced with the help of automatic patterning devices. These devices select needles.<br>\r\n<span class=\"yellow_highlight\"><h3>Selected needles + Carriage settings = Stitch Patterns</h3></span></div></div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n\r\n\n\n<hr class=\"legacy-compat-block-sep\" />\n\n<!-- block: About Automatic Patterning on this Machine | HTML 9348 -->\n<style>\r\n    .blog_container {\r\n        border: 1px solid #ccc;\r\n        border-radius: 15px;\r\n        padding-top: 20px;\r\n        padding-right: 20px;\r\n        padding-bottom: 20px;\r\n        padding-left: 20px;\r\n        background-color: white;\r\n        margin: 100px 100px;\r\n    }\r\n\r\n    img.ctr {\r\n        display: block;\r\n        margin-left: auto;\r\n        margin-right: auto;\r\n    }\r\n\r\n</style>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"blog_container\">\r\n    <div class=\"row\">\r\n        <div class=\"col-sm-5 col-sm-offset-1 col-xs-12 text-center\">\r\n            <img class=\"img-responsive ctr\" src=\"/challenge/images/v2/111/learn_dak_logos.png\" width=\"100\"><br><span style=\"font-size:1.5em\">LearnDesignaKnit.com <br>World Class DAK Instruction</span>\r\n        </div>\r\n        <div class=\"col-sm-6 col-xs-12\"><img class=\"img-responsive\" src=\"https://learndesignaknit.com/img/Learn_DesignAKnit.jpg\"></div>\r\n    </div>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n    <div class=\"text-center\">\r\n\r\n        <br>\r\n        <span class=\"handwriting\" style=\"font-size:2em;line-height:120%\">\r\n            Don't just watch videos!<br>Follow along and then open DesignaKnit and put it to use.<br>\r\n        </span>\r\n    </div>\r\n\r\n    <div class=\"row\">\r\n        <div class=\"col-sm-3 col-sm-offset-3 col-xs-12\">\r\n            <ul class=\"bullets margin-100px-left\">\r\n                <li>Challenge yourself</li>\r\n                <li>Learn at your own pace</li>\r\n                <li>Interactive walk-throughs</li>\r\n                <li>Checklists</li>\r\n            </ul>\r\n        </div>\r\n        <div class=\"col-sm-3 col-xs-12\">\r\n            <ul class=\"bullets margin-100px-left\">\r\n                <li>Translated Videos and Content</li>\r\n                <li>Worksheets</li>\r\n                <li>Tools Glossary and Cheat Sheets</li>\r\n                <li>Keep forever courses</li>\r\n            </ul>\r\n        </div>\r\n    </div>\r\n    <div class=\"text-center\"><a class=\"btn btn-default\" href=\"https://learndesignaknit.com/\" role=\"button\">Visit LearnDesignaKnit.com to Master DAK</a></div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n\n\n<hr class=\"legacy-compat-block-sep\" />\n\n<!-- block: How does Automatic Patterning Work? | HTML 9373 -->\n<h1>Don't Skip This!</h1>\r\nYou can carefully slide your carriage off the needlebed to examine the underside.<br><br>\r\nThere's no mystery or magic to how the carriage works! <br>\r\nThe needle butts are directed through channels. Depending on each needle position and your carriage settings, the needles will either pick up yarn and knit or not (forming stitch patterns).<br><br>\r\n<span class=\"handwriting\" style=\"font-size:1.5em\"> Don't be overwhelmed by this geeky stuff ... just follow along to get a general idea of how things work.</span>\n\n<hr class=\"legacy-compat-block-sep\" />\n\n<!-- block: How does Automatic Patterning Work? | VimeoID 9372 -->\n<div class=\"embed-responsive embed-responsive-16by9\"><iframe class=\"embed-responsive-item\" src=\"https://player.vimeo.com/video/799493924\" title=\"How does Automatic Patterning Work?\" allow=\"autoplay; fullscreen; picture-in-picture\" allowfullscreen loading=\"lazy\"></iframe></div>\n\n<hr class=\"legacy-compat-block-sep\" />\n\n<!-- block: Patterning Goals | HTML 9391 -->\n<style>\r\n    .circle {\r\n        width: 25px;\r\n        height: 25px;\r\n        border-radius: 50%;\r\n        box-sizing: border-box;\r\n        text-align: center;\r\n        display: inline-block;\r\n        line-height: 25px;\r\n        background-color: #9E2065;\r\n    }\r\n\r\n    .circle a {\r\n        text-decoration: none;\r\n        color: #fff;\r\n        font-size: 16px;\r\n    }\r\n\r\n    hr.style13 {\r\n        height: 10px;\r\n        border: 0;\r\n        box-shadow: 0 10px 10px -10px #8c8b8b inset;\r\n    }\r\n\r\n    .tab {\r\n        Margin-left: 50px\r\n    }\r\n\r\n</style>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n    <div class=\"col-sm-8 col-xs-12\">\r\n        <h3>What do you want to knit?</h3><br>\r\n        <h4>Use DAK to send Stitch patterns to the SK840</h4>\r\n        <br>\r\n        <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"/challenge/images/v2/111/WORKSHEETS.pdf\"><i class=\"fa fa-download\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> Download printable checklists</a><br>\r\n    </div>\r\n    <div class=\"col-sm-4 col-xs-12\">\r\n        <img class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"300\" src=\"/challenge/images/v2/111/silverlink.jpg\"><br>\r\n    </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n    <div class=\"col-sm-2 col-xs-12\"> <img class=\"img-responsive\" src=\"/challenge/images/v2/111/1.jpg\"> </div>\r\n    <div class=\"col-sm-8 col-xs-12\">\r\n\r\n        <div class=\"row\">\r\n            <div class=\"col margin-10px-bottom\">\r\n                <div class=\"circle\"><a href=\"#\">1</a></div><span style=\"font-size:1.5em\"><b> Knit in a stitch pattern</b></span><br>\r\n                <div class=\"tab\">\r\n                    When you want to knit a rectangle or a swatch with an all-over stitch pattern.<br>\r\n                    Just let DesignaKnit position the motif repeating it to fill the stitches and rows.<br><br>\r\n<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"/challenge/images/v2/111/1 ALLOVER.pdf\"><i class=\"fa fa-download\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> Checklist </a>\r\n                    <div>\r\n                    </div>\r\n                </div>\r\n            </div>\r\n        </div>\r\n\r\n    </div>\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n<hr class=\"style13\">\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n    <div class=\"col-sm-2 col-xs-12\"> <img class=\"img-responsive\" src=\"/challenge/images/v2/111/2.jpg\"> </div>\r\n    <div class=\"col-sm-8 col-xs-12\">\r\n        <div class=\"row\">\r\n            <div class=\"col margin-10px-bottom\">\r\n                <div class=\"circle\"><a href=\"#\">2</a></div><span style=\"font-size:1.5em\"><b> Position a Stitch pattern</b></span><br>\r\n                <div class=\"tab\">\r\n                    When you are knitting a rectangle (or a swatch) and you want to control where the stitch pattern is positioned.\r\n                    <ul>\r\n                        <li>Single Motif</li>\r\n                        <li>Horizontal Border</li>\r\n                        <li>Vertical Border</li>\r\n                        <li>Tile</li>\r\n                    </ul><br><br>\r\n<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"/challenge/images/v2/111/2 POSITION.pdf\"><i class=\"fa fa-download\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> Checklist </a>\r\n                </div>\r\n            </div>\r\n        </div>\r\n    </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<hr class=\"style13\">\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n    <div class=\"col-sm-2 col-xs-12\"> <img class=\"img-responsive\" src=\"/challenge/images/v2/111/3.jpg\"> </div>\r\n    <div class=\"col-sm-8 col-xs-12\">\r\n        <div class=\"row\">\r\n            <div class=\"col margin-10px-bottom\">\r\n                <div class=\"circle\"><a href=\"#\">3</a></div><span style=\"font-size:1.5em\"><b> Knit a garment piece in pattern</b></span>\r\n\r\n                <br>\r\n                <div class=\"tab\"> Integrate a stitch pattern with a garment piece.\r\n                    Use Interactive knitting to both display stitch pattern instructions AND shaping instructions<br><br>\r\n<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"/challenge/images/v2/111/3GARMENT.pdf\"><i class=\"fa fa-download\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> Checklist </a>\r\n                </div>\r\n            </div>\r\n        </div>\r\n    </div>\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n\n\n<hr class=\"legacy-compat-block-sep\" />\n\n<!-- block: <i class=\"fa fa-circle\" style=color:#9F2065;\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> Knit in a Stitch Pattern | HTML 9453 -->\n<style>.circle{\r\nwidth:25px;\r\nheight:25px;\r\nborder-radius:50%;\r\nbox-sizing:border-box;\r\ntext-align:center;\r\ndisplay:inline-block;\r\nline-height:25px;\r\nbackground-color:#9E2065;\r\n}\r\n.circle a{\r\ntext-decoration:none;\r\ncolor:#fff;\r\nfont-size: 16px;\r\n}\r\n</style>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n    <div class=\"col-sm-2 col-xs-12\"> <img class=\"img-responsive\" src=\"/challenge/images/v2/111/1.jpg\"> </div>\r\n    <div class=\"col-sm-8 col-xs-12\">\r\n\r\n        <div class=\"row\">\r\n            <div class=\"col margin-10px-bottom\">\r\n                <div class=\"circle\"><a href=\"#\">1</a></div><span style=\"font-size:1.5em\"><b> Knit in a stitch pattern</b></span><br>\r\n\r\n                When you want to knit a rectangle or a swatch with an all-over stitch pattern.<br>\r\n                Let DesignaKnit position the motif repeating it to fill the stitches and rows.\r\n<br>\r\n<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"/challenge/images/v2/111/1 ALLOVER.pdf\"><i class=\"fa fa-caret-down\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> Print Checklist </a>\r\n            </div>\r\n        </div>\r\n    </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<hr class=\"style13\">\r\n\r\n <div class=\"videopopup\" data-videotitle=\"position_rectangle\" data-vimeoid=\"799677711\">\r\n\t\t<img class=\"img-thumbnail\" src=\"https://i.vimeocdn.com/video/1612504508-fddb85f6383276c645397678871b7734a69ba748a02920fdd749660e177c0d5a-d_1280x720?r=pad\">\r\n\t\t<div class=\"imagecenter text-center\"><button class=\"btn btn-sm\"><i class=\"fa fa-youtube-play fa-2x learn\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i></button></div>\t\t\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n\n\n<hr class=\"legacy-compat-block-sep\" />\n\n<!-- block: <i class=\"fa fa-circle\" style=color:#9F2065;\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> Position a Stitch Pattern | HTML 9454 -->\n<style>.circle{\r\nwidth:25px;\r\nheight:25px;\r\nborder-radius:50%;\r\nbox-sizing:border-box;\r\ntext-align:center;\r\ndisplay:inline-block;\r\nline-height:25px;\r\nbackground-color:#9E2065;\r\n}\r\n.circle a{\r\ntext-decoration:none;\r\ncolor:#fff;\r\nfont-size: 16px;\r\n}\r\n</style>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n    <div class=\"col-sm-2 col-xs-12\"> <img class=\"img-responsive\" src=\"/challenge/images/v2/111/2.jpg\"> </div>\r\n    <div class=\"col-sm-8 col-xs-12\">\r\n        <div class=\"row\">\r\n            <div class=\"col margin-10px-bottom\">\r\n                <div class=\"circle\"><a href=\"#\">2</a></div><span style=\"font-size:1.5em\"><b> Position a Stitch pattern</b></span><br>\r\n\r\n                When you are knitting a rectangle (or a swatch) and you want to control where the stitch pattern is positioned.\r\n                <ul>\r\n                    <li>Single Motif</li>\r\n                    <li>Horizontal Border</li>\r\n                    <li>Vertical Border</li>\r\n                    <li>Tile</li>\r\n                </ul>\r\n<br>\r\n<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"/challenge/images/v2/111/2 POSITION.pdf\"><i class=\"fa fa-download\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> Print Checklist </a>\r\n            </div>\r\n        </div>\r\n    </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<hr class=\"style13\"><Br>\r\n <div class=\"videopopup\" data-videotitle=\"single_motif\" data-vimeoid=\"799905939\">\r\n\t\t<img class=\"img-thumbnail\" src=\"https://i.vimeocdn.com/video/1613056476-6b1039dfcf3199f41abf962d3834e0df07f3fcfc0f00e5613aee5165a154da2e-d_1280x720?r=pad\">\r\n\t\t<div class=\"imagecenter text-center\"><button class=\"btn btn-sm\"><i class=\"fa fa-youtube-play fa-2x learn\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i></button></div>\t\t\r\n</div>\n\n<hr class=\"legacy-compat-block-sep\" />\n\n<!-- block: <i class=\"fa fa-circle\" style=color:#9F2065;\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i>  Knit a Garment in Pattern | HTML 9455 -->\n<style>.circle{\r\nwidth:25px;\r\nheight:25px;\r\nborder-radius:50%;\r\nbox-sizing:border-box;\r\ntext-align:center;\r\ndisplay:inline-block;\r\nline-height:25px;\r\nbackground-color:#9E2065;\r\n}\r\n.circle a{\r\ntext-decoration:none;\r\ncolor:#fff;\r\nfont-size: 16px;\r\n}\r\n</style>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n    <div class=\"col-sm-2 col-xs-12\"> <img class=\"img-responsive\" src=\"/challenge/images/v2/111/3.jpg\"> </div>\r\n    <div class=\"col-sm-8 col-xs-12\">\r\n        <div class=\"row\">\r\n            <div class=\"col margin-10px-bottom\">\r\n                <div class=\"circle\"><a href=\"#\">3</a></div><span style=\"font-size:1.5em\"><b>Knit a garment piece in pattern</b></span>\r\n\r\n                <br>\r\n                Integrate a stitch pattern with a garment piece.\r\n                Use Interactive knitting to both display stitch pattern instructions AND shaping instructions<Br>\r\n<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"/challenge/images/v2/111/2 3GARMENT.pdf\"><i class=\"fa fa-download\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> Print Checklist </a>\r\n            </div>\r\n        </div>\r\n    </div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<hr class=\"style13\">\r\n<div class=\"videopopup\" data-videotitle=\"position_by_piece\" data-vimeoid=\"799990951\">\r\n    <img class=\"img-thumbnail\" src=\"https://i.vimeocdn.com/video/1613234959-7d3704ced03e0d0b3d578a5191a40dde2b3bb6ece4f0a698a5c6a94902b57dde-d_1280x720?r=pad\">\r\n    <div class=\"imagecenter text-center\"><button class=\"btn btn-sm\"><i class=\"fa fa-youtube-play fa-2x learn\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i></button></div>\r\n</div>\r\n\n\n<hr class=\"legacy-compat-block-sep\" />\n\n<!-- block: Exercises | Exercise 9447 -->\n<aside class=\"legacy-compat-gap\" role=\"note\"><strong>Exercise interaction approximated:</strong> “Exercises” (component 9447). Original KIN accordion/exercise UI is not available; tasks are shown as static &lt;details&gt; only.</aside>\n<div class=\"legacy-compat-exercise-list\"><details class=\"legacy-compat-exercise\"><summary><span style=\"font-size:2em\">Knit in a stitch pattern</span> (good for swatches/rectangles with all-over stitch patterns)</summary><div class=\"legacy-compat-exercise__body\"><p><img class=\"img-thumbnail\" src=\"/challenge/images/arrow1.png\" alt=\"\"></p><div style=\"margin-left: 2.5em; font-size:2em\">\r\n\r\n<a data-popupcontentid=\"6171\" class=\"contentpopup\"> <i class=\"fa fa-spinner fa-spin\" style=\"font-size:30px;color:#9F2065\"></i> Step-by-step exercise  <i class=\"fa fa-caret-down\" style=\"color:#9F2065;\"aria-hidden=\"true\"></i></a></div></div></details>\n<details class=\"legacy-compat-exercise\"><summary><span style=\"font-size:2em;\">Position a Stitch pattern </span>(isolated motifs or custom pattern placement)</summary><div class=\"legacy-compat-exercise__body\"><p><img class=\"img-thumbnail\" src=\"/challenge/images/arrow2.png\" alt=\"\"></p><div style=\"margin-left: 2.5em; font-size:2em\">\r\n<a data-popupcontentid=\"6173\" class=\"contentpopup\"> <i class=\"fa fa-spinner fa-spin\" style=\"font-size:30px;color:#9F2065\"></i> Step-by-step exercise  <i class=\"fa fa-caret-down\" style=\"color:#9F2065;\"aria-hidden=\"true\"></i></a></div></div></details>\n<details class=\"legacy-compat-exercise\"><summary><span style=\"font-size:2em\">Knit a Garment Piece in Pattern</span> (all over stitch patterns and isolated motifs)</summary><div class=\"legacy-compat-exercise__body\"><p><img class=\"img-thumbnail\" src=\"/challenge/images/arrow3.png\" alt=\"\"></p><div style=\"margin-left: 2.5em; font-size:2em\">\r\n<a data-popupcontentid=\"6174\" class=\"contentpopup\"> <i class=\"fa fa-spinner fa-spin\" style=\"font-size:30px;color:#9F2065\"></i> Step-by-step exercise  <i class=\"fa fa-caret-down\" style=\"color:#9F2065;\"aria-hidden=\"true\"></i></a></div></div></details></div>\n\n<hr class=\"legacy-compat-block-sep\" />\n\n<!-- block: Bits and Pieces | HTML 9344 -->\n<style>\r\n    hr.style13 {\r\n        height: 10px;\r\n        border: 0;\r\n        box-shadow: 0 10px 10px -10px #8c8b8b inset;\r\n    }\r\n.yellow_highlight {\r\nbackground: linear-gradient(rgba(255,255,255,0) 55%,#ffff00 45%,#ffff00);\r\n}\r\n</style>\r\n\r\nHere are 4 accessories that are needed for automatic patterning.<br><br>\r\nWe will discuss them in detail in the associated techniques sections.\r\n<hr class=\"style13\">\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n    <div class=\"col-sm-5 col-xs-12\">\r\n        <h3>Yarn Separators</h3>\r\n        If your yarn tangles with the round brushes under the carriage, try using the Yarn Separators on each side. This is especially recommended when knitting Fairisle.\r\n\r\n    </div>\r\n    <div class=\"col-sm-6 col-xs-12\">\r\n        <div class=\"videopopup\" data-videotitle=\"punchcard\" data-vimeoid=\"681919546\">\r\n         <figure>   <img class=\"img-thumbnail center-block\" width=\"300\" src=\"/images/glossary/yarn_separator1.png\">\r\n\r\n<figcaption align=\"center\"><br>Yarn Separator</figcaption>\r\n</figure>\r\n\r\n            <div class=\"imagecenter text-center\"><button class=\"btn btn-sm\"><i class=\"fa fa-youtube-play fa-2x learn\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i></button></div>\r\n        </div>\r\n    </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<hr class=\"style13\">\r\n\r\n<h3>Point Cams</h3>\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n    <div class=\"col-sm-5 col-xs-12\">\r\n        <span class=\"yellow_highlight\">Pattern knitting only happens between 2 point cams.</span>\r\n        <ul>\r\n            <li>When setting Point cams at both edges of the knitting, the pattern will be knitted across the entire row. Needles outside of the point cams will not pattern.</li>\r\n\r\n            <li>When knitting isolated motif, position the point cam on each side of where you want the motif to knit, keeping the other sections in plain knitting.</li>\r\n        </ul>\r\n<div class='embed-responsive embed-responsive-16by9'><iframe src='https://player.vimeo.com/video/825599756' frameborder='0' webkitAllowFullScreen mozallowfullscreen allowFullScreen></iframe></div><br>No sound\r\n    </div>\r\n    <div class=\"col-sm-6 col-xs-12\"><figure><img class=\"img-thumbnail center-block\" src=\"/challenge/images/v2/111/point_cams.jpg\"><figcaption align=\"center\"><br>Point Cams</figcaption>\r\n</figure></div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n</div><hr class=\"style13\">\r\n<h3><del>Needle-1 Cam</del></h3>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-sm-5 col-xs-12\">\r\n<b>The needle-1 (N-1) cams are NOT used with DesignaKnit</b>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>The red line of the Needle-1 cam tells the machine where to start and finish the pattern repeat.</li>\r\n<li>Usually, the Needle-1 Cam is put at the center of the needlebed.</li><b>\r\n<li>NOTE:</b> The Needle-1 Cam MUST be placed within the 2 point cams or at either Point Cam. <span class=yellow_highlight\">Do not put it outside the Point Cams</span></li>\r\n</ul></div>\r\n<div class=\"col-sm-6 col-xs-12\"><figure><img class=\"img-thumbnail center-block\" src=\"/challenge/images/v2/111/needle-1.jpg\"><figcaption align=\"center\"><br>Needle-1 Cam</figcaption>\r\n</figure></div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\n\n<hr class=\"legacy-compat-block-sep\" />\n\n<!-- block: Position Pattern on Needlebed | VimeoMultiple 9379 -->\n<h4 class=\"legacy-compat-video-label\">Position Pattern on Needlebed — video 1</h4>\n<div class=\"embed-responsive embed-responsive-16by9\"><iframe class=\"embed-responsive-item\" src=\"https://player.vimeo.com/video/799677711\" title=\"Position Pattern on Needlebed 1\" allow=\"autoplay; fullscreen; picture-in-picture\" allowfullscreen loading=\"lazy\"></iframe></div>\n<h4 class=\"legacy-compat-video-label\">Position Pattern on Needlebed — video 2</h4>\n<div class=\"embed-responsive embed-responsive-16by9\"><iframe class=\"embed-responsive-item\" src=\"https://player.vimeo.com/video/799905939\" title=\"Position Pattern on Needlebed 2\" allow=\"autoplay; fullscreen; picture-in-picture\" allowfullscreen loading=\"lazy\"></iframe></div>\n<h4 class=\"legacy-compat-video-label\">Position Pattern on Needlebed — video 3</h4>\n<div class=\"embed-responsive embed-responsive-16by9\"><iframe class=\"embed-responsive-item\" src=\"https://player.vimeo.com/video/799990951\" title=\"Position Pattern on Needlebed 3\" allow=\"autoplay; fullscreen; picture-in-picture\" allowfullscreen loading=\"lazy\"></iframe></div>\n\n<hr class=\"legacy-compat-block-sep\" />\n\n<!-- block: Position Pattern on Needlebed | HTML 9380 -->\n<style>\r\nhr.style13 {\r\nheight: 10px;\r\nborder: 0;\r\nbox-shadow: 0 10px 10px -10px #8c8b8b inset;\r\n}\r\n .container-border1 {\r\nborder: 2px solid #ccc;\r\nborder-radius: 15px 50px;\r\npadding-top: 20px;\r\npadding-right: 20px;\r\npadding-bottom: 20px;\r\npadding-left: 20px;\r\nbackground-color: white;\r\n}</style>\r\n<style> .container-border1 {\r\nborder: 2px solid #ccc;\r\nborder-radius: 15px 50px;\r\npadding-top: 20px;\r\npadding-right: 20px;\r\npadding-bottom: 20px;\r\npadding-left: 20px;\r\nbackground-color: white;\r\nmax-width: 800px;\r\nmargin: auto;\r\nbackground-color: #DCDCDC;\r\n}\r\nimg.ctr{\r\ndisplay: block;\r\nmargin-left: auto;\r\nmargin-right: auto; }\r\n</style>\r\n\r\n<br>\r\n<hr class=\"style13\">\r\n\r\n<div class=\"container-border1\">\r\n    <div class=\"row align-items-center\">\r\nIt is CRITICAL to have a good understanding of DesignaKnit to work stitch patterning on this machine.<br><br>\r\nThese videos give you an overview of the steps, but <span class=\"yellow_highlight\">we highly recommend learning more about DesignaKnit.<span><br>\r\n      <a href=\"https://learndesignaknit.com/\">  <img class=\"img-responsive ctr\" src=\"/challenge/images/v2/111/learn_dak_logos.png\" width=\"100\"></a>\r\n        <div class=\"col col sm-margin-5px-bottom xs-margin-5px-bottom text-center sm-margin-20px-top\">\r\n            <h1 class=\"text-white font-size44 md-font-size40 sm-font-size36 xs-font-size30 font-weight-600 line-height-60 md-line-height-55 sm-line-height-50 xs-line-height-45 margin-10px-bottom sm-margin-10px-bottom\">Using DesignaKnit Just Got <em>Easier</em></h1>\r\n            <h5 style=\"vertical-align: middle;\" class=\"text-white font-size19 md-font-size19 sm-font-size15 xs-font-size15 font-weight-300 line-height-40 md-line-height-44 sm-line-height-28 xs-line-height-28 margin-5px-bottom sm-margin-5px-bottom\"><br>\r\n                <span class=\"font-size12\"><i class=\"fa fa-circle\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i></span> Videos <span class=\"font-size12\"><i class=\"fa fa-circle\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i></span> Exercises <span class=\"font-size12\"><i class=\"fa fa-circle\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i></span> Practice<br>\r\n\r\n            </h5>\r\n            <h1><a href=\"https://learndesignaknit.com/\"> LEARNDESIGNAKNIT.COM</a></h1>\r\n        </div>\r\n    </div>\r\n</div>\r\n\n\n<hr class=\"legacy-compat-block-sep\" />\n\n<!-- block: Shaping Garment Pieces | HTML 9384 -->\n<h1>Don't Skip This</h1>\n\n<hr class=\"legacy-compat-block-sep\" />\n\n<!-- block: Shaping Garment Pieces | VimeoID 9383 -->\n<div class=\"embed-responsive embed-responsive-16by9\"><iframe class=\"embed-responsive-item\" src=\"https://player.vimeo.com/video/800130992\" title=\"Shaping Garment Pieces\" allow=\"autoplay; fullscreen; picture-in-picture\" allowfullscreen loading=\"lazy\"></iframe></div>\n\n<hr class=\"legacy-compat-block-sep\" />\n\n<!-- block: End Needle Selection | Exercise 9382 -->\n<aside class=\"legacy-compat-gap\" role=\"note\"><strong>Exercise interaction approximated:</strong> “End Needle Selection” (component 9382). Original KIN accordion/exercise UI is not available; tasks are shown as static &lt;details&gt; only.</aside>\n<div class=\"legacy-compat-exercise-list\"><details class=\"legacy-compat-exercise\"><summary><h3>The importance of End needle Selection</h3></summary><div class=\"legacy-compat-exercise__body\"><p><img class=\"img-thumbnail\" src=\"/challenge/images/arrow1.png\" alt=\"\"></p><div class=\"row\">\r\n    <div class=\"col-sm-6 col-xs-12\">\r\n        For easier seaming and neater edges, prevent the end needles from patterning.<br><br>\r\n        Having a tuck or slip stitch on the edge of the knitting distorts the edge.<br><br>\r\n        Use this one little trick for neat edges.\r\n\r\n    </div>\r\n    <div class=\"col-sm-6 col-xs-12\">\r\n        <div class=\"videopopup\" data-videotitle=\"end_needle_selection_singer\" data-vimeoid=\"718396283\">\r\n            <img class=\"img-thumbnail\" src=\"https://i.vimeocdn.com/video/1447361871-3f47a17396f378541f506ba0958036bf05a6270c77a4ed7572588155ce818911-d_1280x720?r=pad\">\r\n            <div class=\"imagecenter text-center\"><button class=\"btn btn-sm\"><i class=\"fa fa-youtube-play fa-2x learn\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i></button></div>\r\n        </div>\r\n    </div>\r\n</div></div></details>\n<details class=\"legacy-compat-exercise\"><summary><h3> End needle Selection on this machine</h3></summary><div class=\"legacy-compat-exercise__body\"><p><img class=\"img-thumbnail\" src=\"/challenge/images/arrow2.png\" alt=\"\"></p><div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-sm-8 col-xs-12\">To prevent the end needles from patterning on this machine, move the <b>Point cams</b> 1-2 stitches from the edge of the knitting. \r\n<Br>\r\n<h3> PLUS . . . .</h3>\r\nMany stitch patterns recommend pulling the end needle next to the carriage all the way out to deal with the end needles. See each stitch technique description.<Br><br>\r\n\t<img class=\"img-thumbnail ctr\" src=\"/challenge/images/v2/111/end_needles_gif1.gif\">\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"col-sm-4 col-xs-12\">\t<img class=\"img-responsive\" src=\"/challenge/images/v2/111/end_needles_gif.gif\"></div>\r\n\r\n\r\n</div></div></details></div>\n\n<hr class=\"legacy-compat-block-sep\" />\n\n<!-- block: <i class=\"fa fa-ban\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> Wrong Way! | HTML 9431 -->\n<style>\r\nimg.ctr{\r\ndisplay: block;\r\nmargin-left: auto;\r\nmargin-right: auto; }\r\n</style>\r\n<h3>As you are knitting in pattern, you may receive this message:</h3>\r\n\r\n\r\n<img class=\"img-thumbnail ctr\" src=\"/challenge/images/v2/111/wrong_way1.jpg\">\r\n<br>\r\n<span class=\"yellow_highlight\">This indicates that the \r\n<span class=\"imagepopup\" data-imagetitle=\"840 carriage sensor (left AND right)\" data-image=\"/challenge/images/v2/111/sensor.jpg\"><b>SENSOR <i class=\"fa fa-question-circle-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i></b></span>\r\ndidn't pass the magnet  on the needlebed.</span>\r\n<br><br>\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-sm-6 col-xs-12\">\r\n<h3>How to fix?</h3>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Note the current row number</li>\r\n<li>Note that the \"traffic light\" is STOPPED</li>\r\n<li>Rip any stitches that may have knit</li>\r\n<li><a data-GlossaryId=\"355\" class=\"glossaryhelp\">Free Pass <i class=\"fa fa-question-circle\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i></a> the carriage to the side indicated</li>\r\n<li>Adjust the row count (if necessary) with the up and down arrows <i class=\"fa fa-arrow-up\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i><i class=\"fa fa-arrow-down\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i><?li>\r\n<li>RESTART  the traffic signal \r\n<img class=\"img-responsive\" src=\"/challenge/images/v2/111/restart.jpg\"><br> Ready to knit</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"col-sm-6 col-xs-12\"><img class=\"img-responsive\" src=\"/challenge/images/v2/111/wrong_way2a.jpg\"></div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n\r\n"
}